I am in my little kitchen.
I put my things away.
The cups stand in the cupboard.
The plates stand on the shelf.
The coffee stands on the table.
It is finally my own kitchen.
I make a cup of coffee.
It is black and very warm.
I stand by the window.
I have the warm cup in my hands.
I look out at the street.
There is snow on the cold street.
It is winter and dark outside.
But here in the kitchen it is bright and warm.
I drink my coffee.
I like my new flat.
